.TITLE "whoami"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Displays the username associated with the current effective user ID. It is used to __verify your identity__ within the shell environment.

.DIV "TLDR"
**whoami**
Prints the name of the user currently logged into the terminal.
> 

.DIV "SUMMARY"
This command is particularly useful when you have switched users using __su__ or __sudo__ and need to confirm which account is active. It is a simpler alternative to running __id -u -n__.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**linux:id** **linux:who** **linux:w**

